Here are some ways to improve your success rate:

* Remove any metallic body armor. This includes gauntlets of power 
and dwarven boots. Metallic armor will drive up your failure rates, 
especially for a wizard. (Note: dragon scale mail, being non-
metallic, may be worn without penalty, so make or wish up some as 
soon as it becomes feasible.)

* Increase your experience level.

* Increase your skill with matter spells (tip: try casting knock 
and/or wizard lock over and over). You may need to level up to get 
enough skill slots, though.

* Wear a robe. This uses up your cloak slot, but you can use 
Magicbane for MR. Your quest artifact also provides MR, but it can be 
stolen by certain enemies, so don't rely on it too much.

Even with all of that, Polymorph will probably still have a nonzero 
failure rate without a robe until XL 21+.



